00:34:02.300 --> 00:34:05.140
Back inside, Andy is going to tell Jim that he's worried.

798
00:34:05.380 --> 00:34:07.000
You know, Pam bosses him around.

799
00:34:07.200 --> 00:34:07.340
He's

800
00:34:07.340 --> 00:34:09.760
really worried that their relationship maybe isn't so healthy.

801
00:34:09.960 --> 00:34:10.520
And he says,

802
00:34:10.520 --> 00:34:12.460
Listen, I know a few things about love.

803
00:34:12.600 --> 00:34:14.620
Horrible, terrible, awful things.

804
00:34:15.240 --> 00:34:15.420
Yeah.

805
00:34:15.660 --> 00:34:17.140
There's a lot to unpack here.

806
00:34:17.700 --> 00:34:23.340
Andy is projecting his own hurt onto Jim because Pam

807
00:34:23.340 --> 00:34:28.860
shot down this idea of using any of Andy's wedding stuff and he thinks Jim was bulldozed.

808
00:34:29.380 --> 00:34:29.640
Right.

809
00:34:29.800 --> 00:34:31.840
So he's turned this into a whole story.

810
00:34:32.200 --> 00:34:32.400
Yeah.

811
00:34:32.560 --> 00:34:37.040
And Jim sees his opportunity now for a day long of pranking.

812
00:34:37.260 --> 00:34:37.680
Yeah.

813
00:34:37.820 --> 00:34:39.660
Because I think Jim's a little offended.

814
00:34:39.660 --> 00:34:41.540
Well, it is ridiculous.

815
00:34:42.360 --> 00:34:42.540
Yeah.

816
00:34:42.940 --> 00:34:44.900
He's making a lot of assumptions.

817
00:34:45.460 --> 00:34:49.060
So now Michael is going to take this info that he got

818
00:34:49.060 --> 00:34:49.640
from Dwight.

819
00:34:49.780 --> 00:34:55.800
He's headed back to Michael Scott Paper Company and he tells Pam to give Ed's tires

820
00:34:55.800 --> 00:34:56.380
a call.

821
00:34:56.700 --> 00:34:57.040
Yeah.

822
00:34:57.380 --> 00:34:58.660
Here's what she needs to say.

823
00:34:58.820 --> 00:35:01.880
She needs to say that Michael Scott Paper Company has fewer clients

824
00:35:01.880 --> 00:35:07.300
so they can spend more time with each of them and also somehow mention she distrusts women.

825
00:35:07.300 --> 00:35:10.040
And he recommends she do it over Indian food.

826
00:35:10.460 --> 00:35:11.760
Pam's like, I'm not going to say that.

827
00:35:11.920 --> 00:35:13.160
Ryan's like, I can get there.

828
00:35:13.280 --> 00:35:14.440
That made me laugh out loud.

829
00:35:15.080 --> 00:35:17.600
This is a little foreshadowing for something that's going to come up

830
00:35:17.600 --> 00:35:22.000
later, which is that Michael takes kind of meticulous, detailed notes about each client.

831
00:35:22.560 --> 00:35:22.940
Meticulous?

832
00:35:22.940 --> 00:35:26.540
Well, he does little details about each one.

833
00:35:26.740 --> 00:35:32.480
I feel like when I saw Michael's Rolodex, Jenna, it reminded me of my note cards.

834
00:35:32.800 --> 00:35:33.240
Oh.

835
00:35:33.860 --> 00:35:38.460
Because I usually put a few words that mean something to me, right?

836
00:35:38.680 --> 00:35:38.900
Mm-hmm.

837
00:35:39.200 --> 00:35:40.620
Now I put it all in a document.

838
00:35:40.620 --> 00:35:43.840
But if you look at my notes, I give myself words that only mean

839
00:35:43.840 --> 00:35:44.500
something to me.

840
00:35:44.720 --> 00:35:46.300
Look next to Jim's talking head.

841
00:35:46.400 --> 00:35:47.040
What does it say?

842
00:35:47.360 --> 00:35:47.640
Boo.

843
00:35:47.640 --> 00:35:47.690
Boo.

844
00:35:49.060 --> 00:35:50.320
Why does it say boo?

845
00:35:50.520 --> 00:35:51.460
You know what that means.

846
00:35:51.480 --> 00:35:52.980
I don't like Jim in this moment.

847
00:35:53.140 --> 00:35:55.900
I think he's being mean to Andy, so I wrote boo.

848
00:35:56.460 --> 00:35:58.700
And then right here, what does that say?

849
00:35:59.180 --> 00:35:59.640
Trophy.

850
00:36:00.080 --> 00:36:01.460
That means something to me.

851
00:36:01.580 --> 00:36:02.420
We'll get to it.

852
00:36:03.260 --> 00:36:05.960
But I was like, oh my gosh, I'm Michael Scott.

853
00:36:05.960 --> 00:36:08.120
I have like a few keywords.

854
00:36:08.120 --> 00:36:15.020
Well, you know, in my early actor days, when I would go to casting offices, I would come home and

855
00:36:15.020 --> 00:36:21.080
I had a little card file, like a Rolodex, where I would write down little notes about anything like

856
00:36:21.080 --> 00:36:21.420
that.

857
00:36:21.640 --> 00:36:23.760
Like, loves chocolate chip cookies.

858
00:36:24.380 --> 00:36:27.580
So that the next time I went into that casting office,

859
00:36:27.580 --> 00:36:30.820
I could have something that might spark a moment of connection.

860
00:36:30.840 --> 00:36:31.700
Yeah, you're like, hi, Tammy.

861
00:36:31.940 --> 00:36:33.660
Had any good chocolate chip cookies lately?

862
00:36:33.920 --> 00:36:34.800
Pretty much.

863
00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:35.280
Yes.

864
00:36:35.280 --> 00:36:35.960
So casual.

865
00:36:35.960 --> 00:36:36.800
Yeah.

866
00:36:37.320 --> 00:36:38.720
Okay, so back to the scene.

867
00:36:38.900 --> 00:36:40.380
I have a little thing I spotted.

868
00:36:40.740 --> 00:36:46.080
At 5 minutes, 9 seconds, there is a poster hanging in the

869
00:36:46.080 --> 00:36:46.980
background of the scene.

870
00:36:46.980 --> 00:36:49.280
It's over to the left of Michael's desk.

871
00:36:49.400 --> 00:36:49.800
It says,

872
00:36:50.140 --> 00:36:50.580
Diversity.

873
00:36:51.420 --> 00:36:58.100
So that poster was made by Phil Shea using the hands of our hair and makeup crew.

874
00:36:58.360 --> 00:37:01.460
Yes, that is their hands and like, I guess their arms, right?

875
00:37:01.580 --> 00:37:01.860
Yes.

876
00:37:01.980 --> 00:37:02.120
Yeah.

877
00:37:02.120 --> 00:37:02.456
Yeah.

878
00:37:02.456 --> 00:37:04.471
So now Pam has a talking head.

879
00:37:04.471 --> 00:37:06.620
They've done their little chant.

880
00:37:06.900 --> 00:37:07.520
Their cheer.

881
00:37:07.900 --> 00:37:09.700
Their morning, you ugly cheer.

882
00:37:09.960 --> 00:37:10.320
Yeah, yeah.

883
00:37:10.680 --> 00:37:12.700
And she just said, listen, she's here.

884
00:37:12.880 --> 00:37:13.880
She's part of this now.

885
00:37:14.020 --> 00:37:14.700
That's right.

886
00:37:14.860 --> 00:37:18.620
And I had a little catch at 5 minutes and 16 seconds.

887
00:37:18.880 --> 00:37:20.260
What's up, background catch queen?

888
00:37:20.700 --> 00:37:22.580
This is an on-my-face catch.

889
00:37:22.780 --> 00:37:23.020
Oh.

890
00:37:23.500 --> 00:37:27.640
Did you notice in this episode that I have a darker, pigmented lip and eye shadow?

891
00:37:28.760 --> 00:37:30.240
It's a much richer color.

892
00:37:30.460 --> 00:37:31.520
No, I did not notice.

893
00:37:31.520 --> 00:37:32.060
Oh my gosh.

894
00:37:32.180 --> 00:37:32.440
Okay.

895
00:37:32.660 --> 00:37:35.160
I noticed because this was a huge thing.

896
00:37:35.380 --> 00:37:38.360
Listen, when you had dark nail polish out of nowhere, I noticed.

897
00:37:38.520 --> 00:37:38.860
I know.

898
00:37:38.860 --> 00:37:40.380
Your lipstick, I didn't quite notice.

899
00:37:40.660 --> 00:37:48.460
We usually alternated between two neutral lip shades, but my makeup artist, Laverne, she said,

900
00:37:48.600 --> 00:37:51.540
I really think we could go a little bolder for Pam.

901
00:37:51.720 --> 00:37:53.540
She made her first sale last week.

902
00:37:53.660 --> 00:37:53.920
Yeah.

903
00:37:53.920 --> 00:37:55.120
She's got her blazer.

904
00:37:55.360 --> 00:37:55.840
Yeah.

905
00:37:56.020 --> 00:37:56.280
Yeah.

906
00:37:56.440 --> 00:38:00.460
So how can we continue to tell the story of her growing confidence?

907
00:38:00.880 --> 00:38:02.520
So we went with a bolder lip.

908
00:38:03.020 --> 00:38:04.060
I like it.

909
00:38:04.220 --> 00:38:04.580
Thank you.

910
00:38:04.580 --> 00:38:07.180
So our next scene is Charles and Dwight.

911
00:38:07.320 --> 00:38:08.880
They're in Charles's office.

912
00:38:09.580 --> 00:38:11.380
Note his shoulders, please.

913
00:38:12.560 --> 00:38:17.200
Also, please note that Rain's entire watch is exposed because his sleeves are too short.

914
00:38:17.260 --> 00:38:17.440
Okay.

915
00:38:17.800 --> 00:38:18.640
Five minutes, 39 seconds.

916
00:38:18.820 --> 00:38:19.020
All right.

917
00:38:19.320 --> 00:38:23.740
So basically, Charles wants to know if Dwight is happy at the company, you know,

918
00:38:23.880 --> 00:38:25.860
and he invites him out to drinks.

919
00:38:26.160 --> 00:38:26.520
Mm-hmm.

920
00:38:26.880 --> 00:38:31.260
So in the background of this scene, you can see Jim, Jenna.

921
00:38:32.060 --> 00:38:33.720
John has angled his computer.

922
00:38:34.580 --> 00:38:38.020
Because he's clearly like surfing the internet or checking email or something.

923
00:38:38.360 --> 00:38:39.380
So while I was

924
00:38:39.380 --> 00:38:43.080
watching this scene, the first time I just watched it just to watch it, then I was like,

925
00:38:43.160 --> 00:38:43.580
wait a second.

926
00:38:44.020 --> 00:38:46.780
John's doing email in the background and the way back.

927
00:38:47.100 --> 00:38:48.080
This scene also

928
00:38:48.080 --> 00:38:52.360
has a line I love when Charles says to Dwight, you're so focused.

929
00:38:52.500 --> 00:38:53.600
And Dwight says, like a wolf.

930
00:38:53.600 --> 00:38:54.060
Thank you.

931
00:38:56.840 --> 00:39:02.140
Well, Rain was asked in an interview what he thought drinks between Dwight and Charles might

932
00:39:02.140 --> 00:39:02.540
entail.

933
00:39:02.720 --> 00:39:03.020
Yeah.

934
00:39:03.380 --> 00:39:04.440
And this was his answer.

935
00:39:04.640 --> 00:39:08.940
He said, probably Charles getting really bored after about eight minutes

936
00:39:08.940 --> 00:39:10.760
and making up an excuse to leave.

937
00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:15.220
He was also asked about his decision to choose Dunder Mifflin

938
00:39:15.220 --> 00:39:17.160
over Michael Scott Paper Company.

939
00:39:17.720 --> 00:39:18.300
What'd he say?

940
00:39:18.560 --> 00:39:25.320
He said, Dwight is loyal to whoever values loyalty the moSt. And in this case, Dunder Mifflin honors

941
00:39:25.320 --> 00:39:27.160
loyalty with an actual paycheck.

942
00:39:27.500 --> 00:39:30.620
And that is why he chose Dunder Mifflin.

943
00:39:31.080 --> 00:39:36.520
I also want to point out in this scene that Charles is still drinking out of his Satequay

944
00:39:36.520 --> 00:39:38.160
steel insulated coffee mug.

945
00:39:38.280 --> 00:39:38.920
I saw that.

946
00:39:38.920 --> 00:39:40.160
And I have to say, I think it's a betrayal.

947
00:39:40.580 --> 00:39:42.540
You're out of the steel business, Charles.

948
00:39:42.860 --> 00:39:43.820
Let it go.

949
00:39:43.820 --> 00:39:46.760
Get a Dunder Mifflin insulated mug already.

950
00:39:47.200 --> 00:39:50.320
What is your attachment to your Satequay steel mug?

951
00:39:50.480 --> 00:39:53.060
You know corporate gave him a mug, but he's not using it.

952
00:39:53.100 --> 00:39:53.880
That's a choice.

953
00:39:54.160 --> 00:39:55.120
That's what I'm saying.

954
00:39:55.460 --> 00:39:55.600
Yeah.

955
00:39:55.960 --> 00:39:57.660
I think Michael knows this guy.

956
00:39:57.920 --> 00:39:59.160
He's a steel man at heart.

957
00:39:59.340 --> 00:39:59.640
Right.

958
00:40:00.080 --> 00:40:02.340
This next scene is amazing.

959
00:40:02.660 --> 00:40:02.960
Mm-hmm.

960
00:40:03.700 --> 00:40:09.320
Michael calls Dwight to ask about Dunder Mifflin's pricing for Ed's tires.

961
00:40:09.740 --> 00:40:09.860
Yeah.

962
00:40:09.860 --> 00:40:11.060
He wants to undercut them.

963
00:40:11.240 --> 00:40:11.460
Right.

964
00:40:11.460 --> 00:40:14.280
And this is when Dwight's internal conflict begins.

965
00:40:14.500 --> 00:40:14.580
Yeah.

966
00:40:14.640 --> 00:40:15.500
He starts to waffle.

967
00:40:15.820 --> 00:40:17.920
Well, because Charles has invited him to drinks.

968
00:40:18.060 --> 00:40:18.320
I know.

969
00:40:18.320 --> 00:40:19.700
Michael never invited him to drinks.

970
00:40:19.800 --> 00:40:20.140
I know.

971
00:40:20.560 --> 00:40:22.820
So he tells Michael something's come up.

972
00:40:22.940 --> 00:40:23.240
Mm-hmm.

973
00:40:23.900 --> 00:40:26.440
And Michael's like, oh my gosh, is it Moe's?

974
00:40:26.560 --> 00:40:27.680
Did you cover up the well?

975
00:40:28.600 --> 00:40:30.060
What is that backstory?

976
00:40:30.280 --> 00:40:31.080
I don't know.

977
00:40:31.200 --> 00:40:33.920
Has Moe's fallen in the well numerous times?

978
00:40:34.200 --> 00:40:38.340
He's probably fallen and been gone for like two days, and then they find him in the well.

979
00:40:38.340 --> 00:40:39.960
I love comedy like that.

980
00:40:40.300 --> 00:40:42.100
It's there, and then it goes away.

981
00:40:42.340 --> 00:40:43.340
Yeah, you just throw it away.

982
00:40:43.880 --> 00:40:45.000
Michael's not getting it.

983
00:40:45.100 --> 00:40:45.840
He's not.

984
00:40:46.080 --> 00:40:48.120
Dwight starts kind of talking in code.

985
00:40:48.520 --> 00:40:51.940
He's kind of like, things are changing fast, and you know.

986
00:40:52.020 --> 00:40:53.220
There's a cool new guy.

987
00:40:53.480 --> 00:40:57.060
And I don't think he'd like it if I helped even my personal hero.

988
00:40:57.600 --> 00:40:59.720
And Michael's like, what are you talking about?

989
00:40:59.900 --> 00:41:00.880
What are you talking about?

990
00:41:00.880 --> 00:41:07.580
So Pam and Ryan have to write on a notepad to help Michael understand what Dwight is saying.

991
00:41:07.820 --> 00:41:11.040
And then Steve as Michael reads the notepad.

992
00:41:11.360 --> 00:41:18.640
All the expressions that come over Steve's face, as Michael figures this out, I was blown away.

993
00:41:18.860 --> 00:41:22.860
I said, give Steve all of the awards, and that's why I drew a trophy.

994
00:41:24.840 --> 00:41:27.720
Seriously, though, this is an amazing performance.

995
00:41:28.080 --> 00:41:29.900
It's so subtle and nuanced.

996
00:41:30.100 --> 00:41:39.580
And Steve, I loved every single thing you did as Michael being clueless, and then not believing the note they're holding up, but then figuring it out, and then being like,

997
00:41:39.640 --> 00:41:41.120
oh my God, and then being betrayed.

998
00:41:41.540 --> 00:41:42.320
Like, all of it.

999
00:41:42.320 --> 00:41:46.920
It is really hard to play realization as an actor.

1000
00:41:47.100 --> 00:41:47.300
Yeah.

1001
00:41:47.500 --> 00:41:49.240
Because you know the information.

1002
00:41:49.240 --> 00:41:50.760
You had to memorize it.

1003
00:41:50.860 --> 00:41:51.920
You had to read the script.

1004
00:41:51.920 --> 00:41:53.360
You know where the scene is going.

1005
00:41:53.620 --> 00:41:53.980
Yes.

1006
00:41:54.200 --> 00:41:59.560
And so to play all of that, it is like one of the hardest things to do as an actor.

1007
00:41:59.800 --> 00:42:02.040
And then to do it comedically, amazing.

1008
00:42:02.040 --> 00:42:02.480
Amazing.

1009
00:42:02.860 --> 00:42:12.500
We got a fan question about this scene from Kelton O, who said, how is it that Pam and Ryan can hear both sides of this phone call?

1010
00:42:12.980 --> 00:42:13.540
Yeah.

1011
00:42:13.980 --> 00:42:16.940
They seem to hear Dwight so clearly through the phone.

1012
00:42:17.480 --> 00:42:23.740
Well, this is very funny, Kelton, because Rain was actually right off camera.

1013
00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:24.560
Yeah.

1014
00:42:24.740 --> 00:42:26.320
Doing his side of the phone call.

1015
00:42:26.460 --> 00:42:28.160
We could totally hear him.

1016
00:42:28.620 --> 00:42:30.340
Rain actually had to come into work that day.

1017
00:42:30.340 --> 00:42:32.120
He did not have anything else to shoot.

1018
00:42:32.400 --> 00:42:36.140
All he did was stand off camera and read his side of the phone call.

1019
00:42:36.700 --> 00:42:37.940
It's actually a thing.

1020
00:42:38.120 --> 00:42:39.960
It's called doing off-camera work.

1021
00:42:40.280 --> 00:42:43.340
And that is often how different sides of a phone call are done.

1022
00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:49.420
We did not have the capability to, like, call into that office.

1023
00:42:49.620 --> 00:42:50.000
Right.

1024
00:42:50.300 --> 00:42:51.460
Like we did upstairs.

1025
00:42:51.460 --> 00:42:53.800
Because it was a closet and a fakie phone.

1026
00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:54.380
Yes.

1027
00:42:54.640 --> 00:43:00.040
I thought I could see how they were cheating it a little, because Michael is kind of holding the phone out.

1028
00:43:00.040 --> 00:43:05.220
So you would assume if he had the volume pretty high up, it's a tiny room that you guys could probably hear.

1029
00:43:05.440 --> 00:43:08.200
We also had a fan catch from Maya R.

1030
00:43:08.640 --> 00:43:10.080
Who said this, Angela?

1031
00:43:10.360 --> 00:43:10.720
What?

1032
00:43:11.240 --> 00:43:12.900
